[72.091314, "o", "00090: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00  ................\\n000000a0: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00  ................\\n000000b0: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00  ................\\n000000c0: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00  ................\\n000000d0: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00  ................\\n000000e0: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00  ................\\n000000f0: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00  ................\\nroot@ce2e7a678869:/app# xxd -g1 -l 256 /app/main.db-wal\\nxxd: /app/main.db-wal: No such file or directory\\nroot@ce2e7a678869:/app#\\n\"\r\n/logs/agent/trajectory.json:139:      \"message\": \"Analysis: The sqlite3 schema and base table are present, but only 5 rows are visible. The WAL file was present initially, but after running PRAGMA wal_checkpoint the file no longer appears. We need inspect whether the WAL was removed/truncated/renamed, and look for any recoverable copies or deleted file handles.\\nPlan: List /app again, search filesystem for database/WAL-related files, check for deleted open files, and inspect mount info for possible overlay lower layer visibility. Also query the db again to confirm row count after the checkpoint.\",\r\n/logs/agent/trajectory.json:140:      \"reasoning_content\": \"We need respond with JSON commands. We discovered after PRAGMA wal_checkpoint maybe WAL deleted? Actually output says no such file. PRAGMA checkpoint caused sqlite to checkpoint and delete/truncate WAL? Wait task says WAL corrupted or encrypted; normal sqlite only sees 5, checkpoint returns 0|0|0 because maybe it ignored WAL? But now file gone. Uh oh. Did the checkpoint delete the WAL? It says xxd /app/main.db-wal no such. Let's inspect. Maybe SQLite detected corruption and ignored WAL? It could have deleted WAL file on checkpoint? Wait the WAL file existed before. sqlite3 normal query read only 5, not checkpoint? 